[00:01.63]易考范文三
[00:04.25]As is vividly portrayed in the above drawing,two men, representing the countryside and the cities respectively, stride forward hand in hand.
[00:17.11]This drawing conveys a clear message that the urban and rural areas should put a high premium on the common development.
[00:25.91]Looking back on the past, nobody can deny the fact that the boom in cities can be attributed,to a large extent, to labor-intensive industries,which owe much to migrant workers in turn.
[00:39.91]From a different perspective, many farmers swarm into the cities,where they can get more job opportunities and better education,with the aim to improve their living standard.
[00:51.50]All in all, both farmers and city residents benefit from the common development.
[00:57.08]Nevertheless, we should not turn a blind eye to the uniqueness of both areas.
[01:02.88]It is true that people in cities enjoy more chances,better pay and more convenient transportation, but meanwhile,they are rather harassed by such problems as higher living costs,pollution and traffic jams.
[01:18.08]In contrast, people in rural areas have better environment to live in,with fresh air to breathe and clean water to drink.
[01:26.28]Yet, prompt medical services and good education may not be available.
[01:31.53]Therefore, drawing on each other's strong points for common progress will help dwellers in both areas better enjoy the advantages while easing concerns caused by the disadvantages.
[01:44.87]Only in this way, will the country's future prosperity be guaranteed.

